## Definition of Done — emit this block, filled in, with every code response

Copy this and mark each line **PASS**/**FAIL** (+ a ≤10-word reason on any FAIL). This emitted evidence
— not a silent "I reviewed it" — is what makes output dependable. The hard-blocker sections have
**no comment override** (a commented-out leak is still a leak).

```
[SELF] concurrency — every unit has an owner + stop condition (or none started)   §1
[SELF] cancellation — deadlines/timeouts on I/O, cancellation propagated          §4
[SELF] errors      — handled exactly once, context preserved, none swallowed      §3
[SELF] leaks       — every resource released on all paths; nothing unbounded      §2
[SELF] log/obs     — structured logs + correlation IDs, no secrets; errors recorded §5-7
[TOOL] {{GATE_CMDS}}
```

**Legend used throughout:** `[TOOL]` = a named check catches it (the hooks run these — you get them
for free); `[SELF]` = **no tool can see it, you are the only gate.** Concentrate your review effort on
the `[SELF]` items.

