## 1. Concurrency & unit-of-work lifecycle
- [ ] Every task/thread/coroutine has an identifiable owner that can await it. No fire-and-forget.
- [ ] Every one has a documented stop condition and cannot block forever.
- [ ] Shared mutable state is synchronized on **all** accesses, or owned by a single unit.
- [ ] Bounded parallelism over unbounded input (no one-task-per-item over a large collection).

## 2. Leaks (resource & memory)
- [ ] Every acquired resource (file, connection, lock, subscription, timer) is released on all paths.
- [ ] Caches/collections that grow with input have a bound (TTL, size cap, eviction).

## 3. Errors
- [ ] No error is discarded silently; each is handled exactly once (propagate **or** log, never both).
- [ ] Error context is preserved when propagating (the original cause is not lost).
- [ ] Failures that are expected are modeled as values/typed errors, not as crashes.
- [ ] Process-fatal exits happen only at the entrypoint, never in library code.

## 4. Cancellation, deadlines & timeouts
- [ ] Every outbound I/O call carries a timeout/deadline.
- [ ] Cancellation propagates to everything the call started, and is honored promptly.

## 5. Structured logging
- [ ] Structured logger with typed fields; message is a stable constant, not interpolated.
- [ ] Levels used correctly; no secrets/PII logged (sensitive types redact themselves).

## 6. Correlation / MDC
- [ ] Request/correlation/trace IDs are seeded at the entry edge and attached to **every** log line
      automatically — not hand-threaded into each call.
- [ ] IDs propagate outbound so downstream logs join the same trace.

## 7. Observability
- [ ] A span per meaningful unit of work; on failure the error is recorded **and** status set.
- [ ] RED metrics (rate, errors, duration); attribute/label cardinality bounded.

## 8. I/O boundaries (HTTP/RPC/servers)
- [ ] Explicit timeouts on servers and clients; graceful shutdown drains in-flight work.
- [ ] Request bodies size-limited; inputs validated before use.

## 9. Configuration & secrets
- [ ] Config validated at startup (fail fast); secrets from env/secret manager, never committed or logged.

## 10. Tooling gate (all `[TOOL]`; the hooks run these)
- [ ] `{{FMT_CMD}}` clean
- [ ] `{{LINT_CMD}}` clean
- [ ] `{{TYPE_CMD}}` clean
- [ ] `{{BUILD_CMD}}` succeeds
- [ ] `{{TEST_CMD}}` passes
- [ ] `{{VULN_CMD}}` reports nothing actionable

## 11. Project layout & dependency injection
- [ ] Clear module boundaries; dependencies injected, not reached for globally; no hidden init side effects.

## 12. Performance (measure first)
- [ ] Optimization claims backed by a benchmark or profile — never guessed. Cold paths left readable.

